.jpg/960px-USACE_Homer_Spit_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kachemak Bay","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.609167,"lo":-151.3475,"d":3990,"ds":"Kachemak Bay (Dena'ina: Tika Kaq’) is a 40-mi-long (64 km) arm of Cook Inlet in the U.S. state of Alaska, located on the southwest side of the Kenai Peninsula. The communities of Homer, Halibut Cove, Seldovia, Nanwalek, Port Graham, and Kachemak City are on the bay as well as three Old Believer settlements in the Fox River area, Voznesenka, Kachemak Selo, and Razdolna.","wpu":"Kachemak Bay","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Sunrise_on_Kachemak_Bay.jpg/960px-Sunrise_on_Kachemak_Bay.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Homer Public Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.643756,"lo":-151.531592,"d":7942,"ds":"The Homer Public Library is located at 500 Hazel Avenue in Homer, Alaska. It serves the communities of the Southern Kenai Peninsula from Ninilchik to the south side of Kachemak Bay. The library, a department of the City of Homer, has six full-time and three part-time staff.","wpu":"Homer Public Library","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Homerlibrary.JPG/960px-Homerlibrary.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pratt Museum","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.645,"lo":-151.549444,"d":8850,"ds":"The Pratt Museum is a regional natural history museum located in Homer, Alaska, with exhibits exploring life around Kachemak Bay in South Central Alaska. The museum's mission is to preserve \"the stories of the Kachemak Bay region\", through \"collections, exhibits, and programs in culture, science, and art\".","wpu":"Pratt Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Prattmuseum.JPG/960px-Prattmuseum.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Yukon Island","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":59.5225,"lo":-151.493333,"d":9830,"ds":"Yukon Island is an island in outer Kachemak Bay, an inlet of the Cook Inlet of south central Alaska. The island is located about 9 miles (14 km) south of Homer. The island is archaeologically sensitive, with a number of sites documenting the prehistory of the bay.","wpu":"Yukon Island","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/Yukon_Island_Main_Site.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"}],"about":{"ds":"Homer (Dena'ina: Tuggeght) is a city in Kenai Peninsula Borough in the U.S. state of Alaska. It is 218 mi (351 km) southwest of Anchorage. According to the 2020 census, the population was 5,522, up from 5,003 in 2010.","wpu":"Homer, Alaska","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Homerfromslough.JPG/960px-Homerfromslough.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}